          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Rational stable homotopy theory is the simple special case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
          %p
            It is a classical fact that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
            of classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            – is considerably more tractable than general
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebraic
            models for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+types"} rational homotopy types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+Sullivan+algebras"} minimal Sullivan algebras
            or equivalently their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual"} dual
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-coalgebras"} dg-coalgebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            i.e. the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            or
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-modules"} dg-modules
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            %em rational stable homotopy theory
            compatible with that of classical rational homotopy theory in that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            adjunction that connects classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            is, under these identifications, modeled by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            from dg-(co-)algebras to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext classical homotopy theory
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext stable homotopy theory
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi spaces
                        %mtd
                          %munderover
                            %mrow
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi Σ
                                  %mn ∞
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟵
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi Ω
                                  %mn ∞
                        %mtd
                          %mi spectra
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext stabilization
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mtext rationally
                        %mtd
                          %mtext dg(co)algebras
                        %mtd
